From: Linux Fieldwork <internal@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] tarfilter: treat NUL and 0 as regular-file types

Python's tarfile module accepts both REGTYPE (b"0") and AREGTYPE
(b"\0") as ordinary regular files. Map the documented REGTYPE selector
and its numeric alias 0 to both accepted encodings so a NUL-flagged
regular payload cannot bypass regular-file exclusion.

This retained patch is internal work. Author identity and submission
metadata must be set by the authorized sender before any external use.
---
 tarfilter | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tarfilter b/tarfilter
--- a/tarfilter
+++ b/tarfilter
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@ class TypeFilterAction(argparse.Action):
         items = getattr(namespace, "typefilter", [])
         match values:
             case "REGTYPE" | "0":
-                items.append(tarfile.REGTYPE)
+                items.extend((tarfile.REGTYPE, tarfile.AREGTYPE))
             case "LNKTYPE" | "1":
                 items.append(tarfile.LNKTYPE)
